BOUNDARY

Synthetic research only.

It does not:
- implement living or biological tissue;
- establish production topology thresholds;
- establish production clustering algorithms;
- execute or modify STAB-18-R1;
- spend canonical scientific execution;
- authorize runtime activation.

EVIDENCE CLASS TARGET

SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

TOPOLOGY OBJECT

Each member has:

- latent true subfamily;
- observed subfamily label;
- boundary confidence;
- evidence epoch.

Primary calibrated topology confidence:

P(observed label is correct | confidence bin)

is approximately calibrated on held-out synthetic worlds.

The topology object therefore carries:

{
    partition_epoch,
    observed_label,
    boundary_confidence,
    calibration_status
}

A topology label with:

calibration_status != VALID

may not be treated as:
proof-quality partition evidence.

PRIMARY ECOLOGY

Family size:
80..120.

True subfamilies:
4..6.

Active fraction:
30%, 60%, 90%.

Evidence price:
1, 2, 4.

Observed label-noise regimes:

0%,
10%,
25%,
40%.

Local-subfamily drift prevalence:
high enough to stress containment.

Additional regimes:
coherent family,
cross-boundary sparse drift,
whole-family coherent change.

3,000 worlds per:
activity x price x topology-noise primary cell.

Primary topology-noise focus:
10% and 25%.

POLICIES

A — HARD-PARTITION EFFECT

H141 EFFECT-TYPED comparator.

Observed subfamily labels are trusted as hard boundaries.

A valid within-subfamily certificate may authorize the entire observed subfamily.

B — CORE-QUARANTINE

Define high-confidence core:

boundary_confidence >= 0.80.

Subfamily action may affect only:
high-confidence members
of the trigger's observed subfamily.

Low-confidence boundary members are:
quarantined from broadcast.

They may be:
audited individually,
left unresolved,
or handled by a later action.

The certificate is calculated only over:
the action core.

C — BOUNDARY-AUDIT

Before subfamily broadcast:

audit a small set of the lowest-confidence boundary members
plus:
the ordinary within-core certificate.

If boundary disagreement appears:
shrink to CORE-QUARANTINE
or LOCAL.

D — OVERLAP-GUARD

Ambiguous members with:
0.50 <= confidence < 0.80

are treated as belonging to:
an overlap zone.

They are not automatically promoted by either adjacent subfamily.

A subfamily action may proceed on:
the certified core,

while the overlap zone remains:
local / unresolved.

E — TOPOLOGY-TYPED

Requires:

- current topology epoch;
- calibrated boundary confidence;
- action core satisfying boundary-confidence threshold;
- epistemic certificate for the action core;
- explicit quarantine of members outside the justified boundary.

If topology calibration is absent or stale:
subfamily action is inadmissible.

Fallback:
LOCAL.

F — FULL-FAMILY

Reference full audit.

PRIMARY TOPOLOGY CONFIDENCE GENERATOR

Correctly labeled members:

confidence concentrated high.

Mislabeled members:

confidence concentrated low.

Primary calibration target:

high-confidence core mislabel rate:
approximately <=5%.

This is a synthetic working target,
not a production threshold.

UN-CALIBRATED / ADVERSARIAL STRESS

Separate stress breaks the confidence-label relation:

wrong labels can receive high confidence.

In that stress:

TOPOLOGY-TYPED must:
reject the calibration state
or:
lose its guarantee.

No free trust is allowed.

PRIMARY METRICS

1. mean net value;
2. 1st-percentile net;
3. evidence audits/event;
4. active weighted coverage;
5. false-promotion rate;
6. subfamily action rate;
7. local fallback rate;
8. quarantined active value;
9. boundary-audit cost;
10. cross-boundary false promotion;
11. topology-invalid action count;
12. action-core size;
13. value recovered per audited member.

PRIMARY ACCEPTANCE SHAPE

The proof-bearing-topology thesis is supported if:

- TOPOLOGY-TYPED has zero topology-invalid actions in calibrated current-epoch primary conditions;
- CORE/OVERLAP quarantine materially lowers false promotion as label noise rises;
- useful subfamily action survives at 10% and 25% topology noise;
- active coverage remains materially above LOCAL-only in at least some noisy cells;
- evidence remains below FULL-FAMILY;
- BOUNDARY-AUDIT improves the false-promotion / coverage frontier relative to trusting hard labels;
- a stale or uncalibrated topology state causes rejection or locality rather than confident subfamily broadcast;
- no policy claims topology validity from confidence scores whose calibration has been deliberately broken.

FAILURE CONDITIONS

Treat H142 as mixed/negative if:

- topology-aware policies collapse to local action almost everywhere;
- quarantine removes nearly all useful coverage;
- boundary audit costs approach full-family evidence;
- confidence does not predict boundary correctness strongly enough to help;
- adversarial miscalibration passes as valid;
- overlap handling merely hides false promotion in an unmeasured unresolved pool.

ROBUSTNESS

Label noise:
0%, 10%, 25%, 40%.

Boundary-confidence threshold:
0.70, 0.80, 0.90.

Subfamily imbalance:
low, medium, high.

Cross-boundary drift:
5%, 10%, 20% of affected members.

High-value boundary member:
present / absent.

Topology epoch:
current / stale.

Calibration:
valid / shifted / adversarial.

Evidence-price shock:
0.5 -> 8.

OUT-OF-BOX EXTENSION

If H142 succeeds,
topology becomes:

A VERSIONED,
CALIBRATED,
CHALLENGEABLE
MODEL OBJECT.

Possible later operations:

- split a subfamily when repeated boundary dissent accumulates;
- merge neighboring subfamilies when their residual dynamics become exchangeable;
- maintain overlapping memberships during uncertain transitions;
- hibernate weak topology hypotheses rather than deleting them;
- regenerate partitions after damage from surviving local relational evidence.

